WEBVTT

NOTE title: Atlas checkout redesign - weekly sync #1
NOTE meeting_date: 2026-03-02
NOTE series: atlas-checkout

1
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:12.850
<v Maya Chen>Okay, let's get started. Thanks everyone. Agenda today is the checkout redesign scope, the payment provider question, and the timeline for the beta.</v>

2
00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:23.650
<v Daniel Okafor>Sounds good. Before we dive in, quick heads-up that two of my engineers are out Thursday and Friday, so capacity is a bit thin this week.</v>

3
00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:29.830
<v Maya Chen>Noted. So first, scope. Priya, where are we on the new checkout flow designs?</v>

4
00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:36.400
<v Priya Raman>The single-page flow is about eighty percent done. The address autocomplete screens still need work.</v>

5
00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:40.280
<v Priya Raman>I'll have the full mockups ready by Wednesday.</v>

6
00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:46.080
<v Maya Chen>Great. Lucas, did you get a chance to look at the drop-off data?</v>

7
00:00:46.880 --> 00:01:01.880
<v Lucas Ferreira>Yeah, roughly thirty-eight percent of users abandon at the shipping step. Mobile is worse, closer to forty-five. I haven't split it by country yet though. Let me dig into the country breakdown and I'll share it in the channel.</v>

8
00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:04.680
<v Maya Chen>That would be really useful.</v>

9
00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:11.630
<v Daniel Okafor>Forty-five percent on mobile is pretty brutal. That lines up with the support tickets Sofia mentioned.</v>

10
00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:23.200
<v Sofia Alvarez>Right, a lot of the complaints are about the promo code field resetting when you go back a step. Honestly I think that bug alone is costing us.</v>

11
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:30.920
<v Daniel Okafor>Hmm, I wasn't aware it was that bad. I'll take a look at the promo code reset bug.</v>

12
00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:40.180
<v Maya Chen>Thanks. Okay, payment provider. We've been going back and forth between staying on Stripe and moving to Adyen for the European markets.</v>

13
00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:52.520
<v Daniel Okafor>My view hasn't changed. Migrating now adds at least three weeks, and we'd be doing it in the middle of the redesign. That's a real risk to the beta date.</v>

14
00:01:53.320 --> 00:02:02.940
<v Lucas Ferreira>The fee difference for EU cards is about zero point three percent. I'll be honest, I don't think it matters much at our current volume.</v>

15
00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:10.660
<v Maya Chen>Okay. So let's go with Stripe for the beta and revisit Adyen in Q3. Everyone okay with that?</v>

16
00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:13.460
<v Priya Raman>Works for me.</v>

17
00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:16.260
<v Daniel Okafor>Agreed.</v>

18
00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:30.520
<v Maya Chen>Great, decision made. Stripe for the beta, Adyen revisit in Q3. Daniel, can you write up a short note on what an Adyen migration would actually involve, so we have it ready for Q3 planning?</v>

19
00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:35.170
<v Daniel Okafor>Sure, I can do that by end of next week.</v>

20
00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:40.200
<v Maya Chen>Perfect. Last topic, the beta timeline. We told leadership March 23rd.</v>

21
00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:57.540
<v Daniel Okafor>That's tight but doable if the designs land this week. The thing I'm worried about is the address validation API. We're still waiting on the vendor to give us production credentials. Until we have those we can't test the autocomplete end to end.</v>

22
00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:00.340
<v Maya Chen>Who's the contact there?</v>

23
00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:05.750
<v Daniel Okafor>It's someone named Arjun on their partnerships team. I've emailed him twice.</v>

24
00:03:06.550 --> 00:03:10.020
<v Maya Chen>Okay, I'll escalate it with their account manager today.</v>

25
00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:20.820
<v Sofia Alvarez>On the QA side, I need the staging environment refreshed before I can start the regression suite. Right now it still has the old checkout build.</v>

26
00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:25.460
<v Daniel Okafor>Yeah, that's on us. We'll get staging refreshed by Wednesday.</v>

27
00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:32.030
<v Sofia Alvarez>Great. Then I should be able to have the regression pass done by next Monday.</v>

28
00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:40.520
<v Maya Chen>Lucas, one more thing. For the beta, we need a dashboard tracking conversion by step. Could you set that up?</v>

29
00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:50.550
<v Lucas Ferreira>Yeah, I can probably get a first version together, but it might not be before the beta. Let me see what I can do.</v>

30
00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:53.660
<v Maya Chen>Even a rough one is fine.</v>

31
00:03:54.460 --> 00:04:04.460
<v Priya Raman>One concern from my side, if the address autocomplete screens change again after this week, we'll have to redo the usability test, and that pushes everything.</v>

32
00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:11.800
<v Maya Chen>Fair. Let's freeze the design after Wednesday's review. Any changes after that go to the post-beta backlog.</v>

33
00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:14.600
<v Daniel Okafor>Good call.</v>

34
00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:30.780
<v Maya Chen>Okay, to recap. Priya has mockups by Wednesday, Daniel looks at the promo bug and writes the Adyen note, I'm chasing the address vendor, and Sofia starts regression once staging is refreshed. Lucas has the country breakdown and the dashboard.</v>

35
00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:33.890
<v Maya Chen>Thanks everyone, see you next Monday.</v>
